      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community hosts an annual Folk Fair that partners with the Virginia Peach Festival, celebrating local music and produce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadows_of_Dan%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Meadows of Dan sits along Virginia’s Crooked Road, the heritage music trail that showcases old‑time and bluegrass traditions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadows_of_Dan%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cockram Mill and Mayberry Presbyterian Church are listed on the National Register of Historic Places, preserving 19th‑century architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadows_of_Dan%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first visitor kiosk, dedicated in March, displays local music history and streams samples from regional performers.",
